error[V0203]: `Session` cannot be compared with `==`, because of its field `handle`
  --> crates/varyk/tests/fixtures/errors/v0203_compare_blocked/main.vr:11:20
   |
11 |     println!("{}", a == b);
   |                    ^^^^^^ `Session` cannot be compared with `==`, because of its field `handle`
   |
   = note: `Handle` is a Rust type whose `.rs` file does not derive `PartialEq` for it; write `#[derive(PartialEq)]` above it there, or add `PartialEq` to its `#[derive(..)]` list (Varyk reads only `#[derive(..)]`, not a hand-written `impl`)
   = note: in Rust terms, `==` and `!=` need the type to implement `PartialEq`, which Varyk derives for a struct or enum whose every field and payload has it, and reads from `#[derive(..)]` on a Rust type
